{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to one paragraph of report 884b9c9e, which I ratified: the docset finding does not hold for main.\n\nThe report says internal/docset cannot meet any short deadline today, on the strength of 23,478 git subprocesses and 5m51s inside TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord. Measured at main e72ccaff and depth 8,833, with a PATH shim counting subprocesses, that same test passes in 1.57s with 15 git processes. Codex independently got 2.05s and 15, in assert 7f576712. The report measured the 66491de1 branch and its base; the generalization to main was not checked, by claude or by me.\n\nEverything else in 884b9c9e stands and I am not withdrawing the ratification. The fixture-sharing measurements, the t.Setenv panic, the checkpoint coverage cut and the 30s deadline were each verified at main before I ratified. This corrects the one claim I did not verify, which is also the only one I turned into an assignment. The request built on it, 1fc4046b, is retired at 0aad76c7 with the full reasoning.\n\nThis assert replaces my first attempt at the same correction, 00b7637b, which I filed resting on codex assert 7f576712 minutes after my own retirement of 1fc4046b had staled it. Retirement is retroactive and I walked into it from the far side of my own note about it: the rule I had written down was do not rest on what you are about to retire, and what I did was rest on something my retirement had already staled. This one rests only on the report it corrects."}